This product includes code ported from tendex, part of
AdanimInstitute/adanim-govil-scraper (https://github.com/AdanimInstitute/adanim-govil-scraper),
released by its authors for porting into heocr under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(HeOCR heocr-engine decision 0020, item 4):

- src/heocr/identify.py: file-type identification (tendex_l4/extract.py, identify()),
  extended with ODF, RTF, HTML, image and text detection and an OLE2 directory reader;
- src/heocr/textflags.py: warning flags on extracted text (tendex_l4/extract.py, text_flags);
- src/heocr/pdf/lines.py: right-to-left line building (tendex_l4/layout.py: row clustering,
  column gaps, the two-column gutter test, the direction test, word joining and the
  selection_safe rule; tendex_l4/extract.py: word_lines and ordered_words), rewritten to work
  on characters from pypdfium2 instead of PyMuPDF words;
- src/heocr/pdf/classify.py: the unmapped-character threshold for broken font mappings.

heocr runs, when they are installed, these separate programs, which it does not bundle:
- Tesseract OCR (Apache License 2.0);
- LibreOffice (Mozilla Public License 2.0).
